# 🚀 AI Customer Support Copilot — Implementation Plan

## Overview

Build a scalable SaaS-based AI Customer Support Copilot using **Node.js, React.js, PostgreSQL, Sequelize ORM, Socket.io, and Ollama** (local AI). The platform enables businesses to manage customer conversations in real-time with AI-powered agent assistance.

---

## User Review Required

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **Ollama Dependency**: The AI features require [Ollama](https://ollama.com/) running locally with `llama3` or `mistral` models pulled. AI features will gracefully degrade if Ollama is unavailable.

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **PostgreSQL Required**: You must have a PostgreSQL instance running locally (default: `localhost:5432`). The plan assumes database name `ai_support_db` with user `postgres`.

> [!WARNING]
> **Tailwind CSS**: Your spec requests Tailwind CSS. I'll use **Tailwind CSS v3** via CDN/PostCSS for the React frontend. Please confirm if you'd prefer a different version.

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **Phased Delivery**: Due to project size, I'll implement in **3 phases** as per your MVP roadmap. Phase 1 will be built first, then Phase 2 and 3 after your review.

